everse transcriptase</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2008</year><volume>453</volume><fpage>184</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18464735</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Prats</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Sarih</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Gabus</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Litvak</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Keith</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Darlix</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Small finger protein of avian and murine retroviruses has nucleic acid annealing activity and positions the replication primer tRNA onto genomic RNA</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><year>1988</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>1777</fpage><lpage>83</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2458920</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barat</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Lullien</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Schatz</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Keith</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Nugeyre</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Gr&#x000fc;ninger-Leitch</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Barr&#x000e9;-Sinoussi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>LeGrice</surname><given-names>SF</given-names></name><name><surname>Darlix</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>HIV-1 reverse transcriptase specifically interacts with the anticodon domain of its cognate primer tRNA</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><year>1989</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>3279</fpage><lpage>85</lpage><pub-id pub-id